<title>FRANCE: EU cuts maize import tariff to Portugal.</title>
<headline>EU cuts maize import tariff to Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday awarded a tariff cut of 39.25 Ecus per tonne for imports of 150,000 tonnes of maize into Portugal, the full quota set aside for that destination, European grain officials said.</p>
<p>The preferential imports come under a long standing agreement to compensate the U.S. and other maize exporters for losses after Portugal joined the European Union. The maize is normally imported from the United States.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
